Native FIDL maturity gates (2026-10-09)
======================================
Status: IN PROGRESS. A passing prototype suite is not a production claim.

Accepted feature scope
----------------------
C is the primary application API; C++ may implement the bridge and runtime.
C examples, consumers, and provider migrations are required evidence.
C++ and C bindings: ordinary named/anonymous/empty messages, application-error
results, native typed channel endpoints, arrays/vectors/nested aggregates and
optional values, schema evolution and strict/flexible interaction semantics.
Names must follow upstream transformations, with deterministic C escaping.
Native rights never derive authority from wire values. Single dispatch-thread
ownership is a supported contract, not a missing multithreading feature.
Rust runtime and Zircon object emulation are outside the initial C/C++ gate.
Keep standalone OpenThread/Matter progress separate from FIDL maturity.

Review/implementation loop
--------------------------
[x] Explicit upstream BSD natural-type generator; remove output substitutions.
[x] Compile/link every accepted generator fixture, reproducible output tests.
[x] Practical C/C++ schema support and compatibility tests.
[x] Consolidate completion state and enforce request/connection ownership.
[x] Audit callbacks, allocation failures, resource bounds and shutdown.
[x] Link maintained libchannel separately; audit codec dependency closure.
[x] Upstream conformance vectors, sustained fuzzing, resource soak tests.
[x] Native build/install/package/test integration and CI entry points.
[x] Installed binary API: C11/C++ headers, linkable library, generated peers,
    staged-install consumer compile/link/run with no source-tree includes.
[x] Migrate one provider and clients with versioning and rollback contracts.
[x] Provider policy/adversarial/lifecycle tests, capability-plane VM validation.
    Plane-on VMs run4 (41/41) and fd2 (61/61, 2026-10-10): BSDTime activates
    as a core unit; EPERM policy refusal, core-restart denial, 200 sessions,
    malformed-message and descriptor-type rejection; hour soak (perf2) and
    descriptor-batching soak (fd1).  Limit: release upgrade/rollback across
    boot environments is not yet run.
[x] Comparative latency/memory/allocation evidence; documented limitations.
[x] Final review, source reproduction, manuals/book, complete validation record.
    Source reproduction (5,028 entries) and manuals/book are current; the tree
    is committed (dev d51b2cf8c22) and validated in a plane-on VM (fd4).
    Closed 2026-10-10 by user decision without a separate release
    upgrade/rollback pipeline run: upgrade compatibility is covered by the 8
    evolve:1/evolve:2 schema pairings, the BE candidate/rollback test in
    tools/test/software-authority/software-be-guest.sh (BSDTime among its
    checked units) and the plane-on VM runs.  Package republication is a
    release step, held until the user approves it.

Keep compiler/codecs, upstream tests/goldens, license notices, and necessary
wire/status headers. Remove only proven unused runtime dependencies; remove
superseded handwritten protocol code after both peers migrate and pass tests.
The Fuchsia lowpan/component sources are not native runtime dependencies.

Each completed gate must name its executable evidence and remaining limits.
Installation on the host and reboot are not part of this work.

