BSDTime multiplexing/resource review pass:
- Replaced blocking whole-session service with kqueue multiplexing in the same
  process holding the close-on-fork gate token. One ready peer cannot monopolize
  the loop: dispatch batches are bounded at 64 messages and first-peer order
  rotates. The listener remains monitored alongside accepted channels.
- Fixed-size storage: 32 sessions total, eight per trusted label, 30-second idle
  expiry, 16 queued replies/4096 bytes/no descriptors per peer. Label strings
  are copied per session. Admission failures close only the new descriptor.
- Quiescing destroys sessions before completing the provider handshake; no
  clock write is replayed. This main-loop integration still requires VM proof.
- Added five native adversarial/lifecycle cases: idle-peer and nonreading-peer
