Boolean vector decode fix and bounded fuzz (2026-10-10)
-------------------------------------------------------
- The natural vector<bool> decoder read an uninitialized local after an
  invalid wire boolean (fuzz-6oemkrlv). fuchsia-natural-bool.patch
  value-initializes both temporaries; a patched empty-staging import matches
  all 4970 contrib/fuchsia entries in content and mode.
- Codec.InvalidBooleanVectorClosesDescriptor rejects a malformed vector<bool>
  carrying a descriptor and proves the descriptor closes. Sanitizer and fuzz
  builds use -ftrivial-auto-var-init=pattern so this read fails
  deterministically; the unpatched header fails the new test under UBSan.
- Ordinary and ASan/UBSan suites: 67 C++ runtime cases plus C11, generator
  and dependency checks pass. The original crash replays clean.
- A 301-second coverage-guided run executed 8264571 inputs with no reports:
  /usr/obj/5bsd-fidl-runtime/fuzz-9e_zdeb2/result.json. This is a bounded
  run, not sustained fuzzing; upstream conformance vectors remain open.

